# Patch 0079 — Local AI runtime bridge (ROADMAP Phase 6; ADR 0013). The
# generation half of the north star's "ask questions about what you kept":
# a single, narrow, auditable path from Kavacha to a local language model,
# and the first feature that rides it. The retrieval half is patch 0078's
# personal index; wiring the two into natural-language history search is the
# next brick, and every later AI feature (tab assistant, ask-my-history)
# reuses this bridge rather than opening its own.
#
# WHAT: KavachaAIBridge.sys.mjs — a stateless process module exposing exactly
# isAvailable(), listModels(), generate(prompt,{model,system,signal}) and
# chat(messages,{model,signal}) over Ollama's REST shape (/api/tags,
# /api/generate, /api/chat), which llama.cpp / LM-Studio / any OpenAI-ish
# local server also speaks. It holds no browser state: a feature gathers its
# own context and passes it in, so what the model sees is always visible at
# the call site. First consumer: a "Summarize This Page" palette command that
# reads the current page's stored text from the personal index (new
# getText(url)) and shows the model's answer in a kavacha-ai arrow panel. AI
# settings get a "Local AI" group in the Privacy Center — enabled toggle,
# endpoint field, model picker, live status — because a feature that reads
# your pages belongs where privacy is managed.
#
# PRIVACY — THE ENDPOINT LINE. kavacha.ai.endpoint defaults to
# http://localhost:11434 and Kavacha NEVER falls back anywhere remote: every
# request is exactly `this.endpoint + path` and nothing else. If the user
# points it at their own hosted model, that is their choice; Kavacha hosts
# nothing and defaults nowhere off-device. Availability is probed ON DEMAND
# only (a short-timeout GET /api/tags when a feature runs or the settings open)
# — never at startup and never in the background, so a fresh idle profile stays
# network-silent (R3). kavacha.ai.enabled (default true, UNLOCKED) is the
# master switch; off means the bridge never touches the network — a disabled
# generate() throws before any fetch. The bridge stores no prompts or
# responses; AI "memory" is a later, explicitly-opt-in feature, not a side
# effect here.
#
# WHY A PATCH, NOT AN OVERLAY: the bridge is an EXTRA_JS_MODULES entry in
# src/zen/common/moz.build (loaded as resource:///modules/), the summarize
# command is a BUILTIN in the command registry, the result panel is a
# <panel> in zen-panels/popups.inc, and getText() is a method on the index
# singleton — all backend registrations an overlay cannot express. A new
# EXTRA_JS_MODULES entry ships only via a full `mach build` (build-only), not
# build:ui.
#
# Verified over Marionette against a mock Ollama server on a real build:
# isAvailable() reports the runtime and lists its models, generate() and
# chat() round-trip, a dead endpoint degrades to {available:false,
# reason:"unreachable"} without throwing, a disabled bridge makes zero
# requests (generate throws before fetch), the "Summarize This Page" command
# fills the panel with the model's summary end-to-end, and the Privacy Center
# "Local AI" group renders status "ready" with the model picker populated from
# the runtime. Real-model quality needs a real model and is out of the
# engineering gate's scope.
#
# Upstream files touched: locales/en-US/.../zen-preferences.ftl,
# locales/en-US/.../zen-command-palette.ftl,
# src/browser/base/content/zen-panels/popups.inc,
# src/browser/components/preferences/kavacha-privacy.js,
# src/browser/components/preferences/kavachaPrivacyCenter.inc.xhtml,
# src/zen/common/moz.build, src/zen/common/sys/KavachaAIBridge.sys.mjs (new),
# src/zen/common/sys/KavachaCommandRegistry.sys.mjs,
# src/zen/kavacha-index/KavachaPersonalIndex.sys.mjs.
